ll, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (2 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "Quick verification against the revised Brief."}}, {"id": "53ac931b-402e-57f5-b283-98877c960bb0", "at": 1795676632.4314015, "until": 1795676634.1824598, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26949, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0db6ce55c0f214eebf3b8a81e399581e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01N2QLVfpb1xxuMNXyWxjVPh", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q && git diff d952caa HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q && git diff d952caa HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900"]], "output": "```console\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n+\n+   *Lineage.* 3b is not a new estimator: it is the model-assisted generalized regression (GREG) estimator of survey sampling (Särndal, Swensson & Wretman 1992; `sarndal1992model`), and PPI++ with a slope fitted on the labelled sample (Angelopoulos et al. 2023). What the study adds is the application (source-model results as the covariate for a new model's score), the choice of s_i, and the controlled analysis of when it helps, above all for targets stronger than all sources.\n+\n+   *Post-results status.* 3b was designed after results-v1 showed the failure of the source-tuned λ on the extrapolation targets; the paper says so. Its specification is fixed before the run: s_i ∈ {source-mean logit, rank-2 low-rank/IRT difficulty}, with or without p̂^{CF}, ridge (small fixed penalty on β1, β2, none on β0) or none; the grid is reported whole and one variant is chosen by the leave-one-benchmark-out rule of the Outline, not by the extrapolation targets. Evidence not tied to the design: 3b is also reported in the interpolation and lineage splits, where it was not motivated, and a cell not used in motivating it (extrapolation targets/draws not examined in results-v1, or the benchmark family held out by the rule) is flagged as the clean test.\n+\n+   *Closest comparator.* \"Stratify on source difficulty and post-stratify/regress\" is the contrast that decides whether 3b adds anything: the (stratified design) × (3b with s_i = source difficulty) cell against (stratified) × (stratum-mean/Hájek) and (uniform) × (3b). The \"about 10% or less over stratified\" of results-v1 is the number this contrast settles; if 3b adds nothing over stratify-and-post-stratify, the paper reports that, and the contribution is the analysis and the robustness claim, not the estimator.\n+\n+   *Small-n rule.* With n = 10–30 and a 0/1 outcome a 2–3 parameter linear fit can leave [0,1] or be unstable. Rule: fitted values are clipped to [0,1]; β is ridge-penalised; if the sample has fewer than 3 items of either class, or the weighted design matrix is rank-deficient, the estimator falls back to the Hájek sample mean. The fall-back rate by n and split is reported next to the error, and results at n where it exceeds 20% are marked as mostly the fall-back.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "3b68b4b1-dbf7-5838-bf20-6ae26bd06d7d", "at": 1795676633.2611444, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26953, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "0db6ce55c0f214eebf3b8a81e399581e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "cda672a0-b744-52da-b254-f3b9fe94c059", "at": 1795676633.2642286, "clock": "host", "stre